></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="16" rect="595.276001,271.915802,779.276001,363.915802"
/></text
><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20250630092851+10'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" inreplyto="04132ccc-9928-496d-ac6f-0dbd95e0d8c3" date="D:20250630092855+10'00'" name="0ab26d48-6703-4855-9f94-3a731fdfbfe1" icon="Comment" page="16" rect="63.218887,339.915802,87.218887,363.915802" subject="Sticky Note" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Sports compression garments appear to enhance measures&#xD;of venous blood flow at rest, during (plus arterial&#xD;measures) and in recovery from a physiological challenge&#xD;(Fig. </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>7</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>). In addition, at immediately after a physiological&#xD;challenge, compression garments did not alter peripheral&#xD;blood flow measures. The findings from this review support&#xD;the mechanism of compression-induced changes in peripheral&#xD;blood flow and highlight that SCG are most beneficial&#xD;when worn during a physiological challenge. However, additional&#xD;high-quality research that addresses the limitations of&#xD;compression garment research highlighted in this review is&#xD;warranted.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="16" rect="595.276001,271.915802,779.276001,363.915802"
/></text
